<title>INDIA: India Haldia Petrochem-financial, product summary.</title>
<headline>India Haldia Petrochem-financial, product summary.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is an an executive summary of Haldia Petrochemicals Ltd, a naphtha-based cracker and petrochemical complex planned at eastern India.</p>
<p>Financial overview:</p>
<p>PROJECT COST:</p>
<p>------------</p>
<p>The total project capital outlay of $1.44 Billion consists of:</p>
<p>				   Rs. Million     USD Million    Pct</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Equity:						     550</p>
<p>Chatterjee Petrochem Co	  4,329		120</p>
<p>WBIDC				  4,329		120</p>
<p>TATA				   1,444		 10</p>
<p>Public Offering/</p>
<p> Private Placement		 9,708		270</p>
<p>									   38.3</p>
<p>Debt:							 886</p>
<p>Indian Financial Institutions  9,500		264</p>
<p>Indian Banks			 4,000		111</p>
<p>Lease Financing			500		 14</p>
<p>Other Local Borrowing	    2,524		 70</p>
<p>Mitsubishi/J-Exim Loan	   4,570		127</p>
<p>Foreign DPG Tranche *	    5,400		150</p>
<p>Foreign Limited Recourse *     5,400		150</p>
<p>									   71.7</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Total Project Costs	     51,704	    1,436     100.00</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>* To be arranged by ANZ Investment Bank</p>
<p>PROJECT OVERVIEW:</p>
<p>Haldia Petrochemicals Limited (&quot;HPL&quot;) is developing a large integrated naphtha-based petrochemical complex at Haldia, West Bengal, India (the &quot;Project&quot;). The products slate consists of:</p>
<p>* 210,000 tpa of Polypropylene (&quot;PP&quot;);</p>
<p>* 200,000 tpa of High Density Polythylene (&quot;HDPE&quot;);</p>
<p>* 120,000 tpa of Linear Low Density Polyethylene (&quot;LLDPE&quot;) (or an equivalent quantity of HDPE, as a swing plant);</p>
<p>* 117,400 tpa of Pyrolysis Gasoline;</p>
<p>* 64,900 tpa of Butadiene.</p>
<p>* 64,500 tpa 0f C4 Raffinate</p>
<p>* 63,700 tpa of Benzene</p>
<p>* 59,800 tpa of Carbon Black Feedstock (&quot;CBFS&quot;);</p>
<p>* 42,400 tpa of C6 Raffinate;</p>
<p>* 3,080 tpa of other products; and</p>
<p>* 95,773 tpa of Ethylene</p>
<p>Source:ANZ Investment Bank.</p>
